  "goodToKnow": "Die Synthese is synthesis: in chemistry (die Synthese von Ammoniak, by Fritz Haber, 1909), in biology (die Photosynthese) and in thinking. German school essays (Erörterungen) often follow These, Antithese, Synthese, a pattern associated with Hegel's dialectics, though Hegel himself rarely used those words. Synthetisch means synthetic. The y is pronounced ü. Plural: die Synthesen."
